# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Fiesta
# Ford Fiesta Mk1: Ford's first supermini, on sale in Europe from September
# 1976 and in the UK (right-hand drive) from January 1977. UK registrations
# rose from 40,934 (1977, its first full year, already in the top ten) to
# 110,753 (1981); the Fiesta was a UK top-ten seller from launch.
#
# Colours: Venetian Red, Midnight Blue, Diamond White, Black. The paint names
# are the actual Mk1 Ford offerings recorded from the Ford Cars brochures
# (Venetian Red 1976-78, Midnight Blue 1977-79, Diamond White 1976-83, Black
# 1976-83). The DVSA colour table starts at 1994 registrations, so its 1994-96
# survivor shares (blue 23-25%, red 19-23%, white 7-10%, black 8-10%) are the
# measured base, adjusted for 1970s registrations, where red and white were
# stronger: red raised to 27%, white to 14%, blue lowered to 22%, black 9%.
#
# Dates describe when that colour would be seen regularly on UK roads, not the
# production dates. Weights total 500, the 2026-11-15 anchor convention for the
# Fiesta (provisional; a central rebase follows), split 27:22:14:9.

